WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.280
$750 million traded on 2026 elections is now part of a CFTC swap proposal. This is Prediction

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:14.760
Markets Daily, episode 25. Journalism and education, never a bet. CNN put that combined kalshi

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:20.560
and polymarket figure together from public data and published the read on September 24. CNN

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:25.920
has a partnership with kalshi and uses kalshi data in its coverage. This show takes no money

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:27.960
from any venue and holds no position.

00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:34.740
The anti-corruption data collective, current through September 30, counts $221 million already

00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:36.480
placed on congressional contracts.

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:43.440
That count covers 21,811 markets on Polymarket, Polymarket US, and Calche.

00:00:43.950 --> 00:00:49.980
The entire 2024 congressional cycle on the same group's tally was $92.4 million.

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:56.840
dollars. The collective projects $1.4 billion to $1.6 billion for the full 2026 cycle.

00:00:57.400 --> 00:01:03.160
An August report from the group found that only 8% of the eventual 2024 total was in at the

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:09.140
comparable point, and that share is what produces the high end of the range. Senate races in Texas,

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:15.900
Maine, Michigan, and South Carolina, plus Kentucky's fourth, each draw several times the next race down.

00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:21.100
Many closely watched house battlegrounds had less than $100,000 of volume.

00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:26.020
Contracts on which party will control Congress had drawn a combined $32 million.

00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:30.620
16% of this cycle's congressional markets are about who wins.

00:01:31.180 --> 00:01:37.340
58% are about the margin. In 2024, 71% of election markets were on the winner.

00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:41.980
Reuters reported from the collective's data. Researcher Michelle Kendler

00:01:41.980 --> 00:01:46.760
Cratch told Reuters that most of the money is still on who wins, and that a lot of the

00:01:46.760 --> 00:01:48.500
stranger markets barely trade.

00:01:49.060 --> 00:01:54.140
Calche has suspended at least 6-26 candidates this year for trading their own races.

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:55.540
CNN reported.

00:01:56.200 --> 00:02:01.900
A polymarket spokesperson told Reuters the company's election markets show a 98% accuracy rate

00:02:01.900 --> 00:02:02.700
one day out.

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:07.400
Benjamin Freeman, who runs politics growth at Calche, told CNN,

00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:10.420
Then, election prediction markets are well calibrated.

00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:16.480
On October 9th, the CFTC proposed defining event contracts as swaps, and the list in

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:20.000
that proposal covers sports, politics, culture, and weather.

00:02:20.600 --> 00:02:25.320
Chairman Michael Selig said in the announcement that the products are within the agency's exclusive

00:02:25.320 --> 00:02:26.000
jurisdiction.

00:02:26.620 --> 00:02:32.380
A companion interim rule keeps wagers on US sportsbooks and casino games outside that definition.

00:02:32.380 --> 00:02:39.280
A Reuters' Ipsos poll taken from September 30 through October 5 found 60% of US adults

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:42.260
opposed to using these markets to wager on election results.

00:02:42.820 --> 00:02:46.440
13% supported that use, and 24% were not sure.

00:02:47.614 --> 00:02:52.654
Mike Selig in a Friday post reported by Token Post described the exchanges as businesses

00:02:52.654 --> 00:02:56.474
that match by and sell quotes from customers in more than one state.

00:02:56.954 --> 00:03:01.894
He said Congress authorized the agency to set uniform standards, watch for fraud and

00:03:01.894 --> 00:03:07.014
manipulation, act on those practices, and protect customer funds across state lines.

00:03:08.049 --> 00:03:12.689
SpaceX is back in front of Anthropic on a polymarket contract about which company

00:03:12.689 --> 00:03:17.349
posts the largest initial public offering by Market Value in 2026.

00:03:18.169 --> 00:03:26.009
Token post read that contract at 5 in the morning Eastern on Saturday, 64% for SpaceX, 35.9%

00:03:26.009 --> 00:03:26.929
for Anthropic.

00:03:26.929 --> 00:03:32.209
The move followed an October 14th investor meeting in San Francisco, where some people

00:03:32.209 --> 00:03:34.909
discussed evaluation near $1.5 trillion.

00:03:35.609 --> 00:03:40.889
That talk was down from about $2 trillion previously expected for a November share sale.

00:03:41.509 --> 00:03:46.189
And Thropic told prospective investors that third quarter revenue hit $16.8 billion.

00:03:46.809 --> 00:03:51.329
That was up 45% from $11.6 billion in the second quarter.

00:03:51.329 --> 00:03:57.429
2nd quarter revenue itself had climbed from $4.7 billion in the first quarter, and

00:03:57.429 --> 00:04:00.909
THROPPIC also reported adjusted profitability in the 3rd quarter.

00:04:01.429 --> 00:04:06.149
The contract scores SpaceX on the first trading days close, not the offering price.

00:04:06.729 --> 00:04:13.009
Those shares were priced at $135 and closed June 12th at $160.95.

00:04:13.549 --> 00:04:17.809
That close put the company near $2.1 trillion of market value.

00:04:17.809 --> 00:04:23.789
A figure near $1.77 trillion is the value at the offering price, which is a different

00:04:23.789 --> 00:04:24.329
benchmark.

00:04:24.969 --> 00:04:30.769
Token Post's point is that a $1.5 trillion discussion by itself does not settle whether

00:04:30.769 --> 00:04:33.569
Anthropic could clear SpaceX's first-day value.

00:04:34.453 --> 00:04:37.833
Kevin Warsh would not preview the October 28th rate decision.

00:04:38.253 --> 00:04:44.173
He said so on October 16th at an International Monetary Fund Fireside Chat in Bangkok, and

00:04:44.173 --> 00:04:45.933
he said he does not prejudge meetings.

00:04:45.933 --> 00:04:52.813
FinBolds reading of Polly Market reported by KuCoin put no change at 87% and called that

00:04:52.813 --> 00:04:54.653
an all-time high for the contract.

00:04:55.013 --> 00:05:02.273
A 25 basis point hike was at 14%, reported volume was 13.15 million dollars on no change

00:05:02.273 --> 00:05:04.953
and 9.97 million dollars on the hike.

00:05:05.633 --> 00:05:12.273
On September 16, the Federal Reserve raised the target range by 25 basis points to 3.75%

00:05:12.273 --> 00:05:19.253
through 4%. Finn Bulld also reported 96.8% on zero rate cuts by the end of 2026.

00:05:19.933 --> 00:05:24.953
A Los Angeles Restaurant Group used a $60,000 Dodgers contract to hedge playoff risk.

00:05:25.473 --> 00:05:31.302
Cal she told Reuters on October 16th. The NBA and the WNBA announced a responsible

00:05:31.302 --> 00:05:35.182
gaming campaign on Tuesday with the National Council on Problem Gambling.

00:05:35.742 --> 00:05:39.262
The campaign is meant to teach fans about risks tied to sports betting.

00:05:39.262 --> 00:05:44.682
The same day, 11-time All-Star, Nekka Agoumike, said at a summit in Santa Barbara.

00:05:45.102 --> 00:05:50.262
It's not a safe place for athletes. She said players are struggling with hostility aimed at how

00:05:50.262 --> 00:05:56.742
they play. League and union resources exist, she said, and they do not stop every incident. Some of

00:05:56.742 --> 00:06:03.122
those experiences may change how players perform, she said. Token Post reported a 2025 finding that more

00:06:03.122 --> 00:06:08.222
than half of Division 1 men's basketball players had faced online harassment tied to their play.

00:06:08.222 --> 00:06:14.702
46% named a better who had a wager on one of their games as a source of negative or threatening messages.

00:06:15.451 --> 00:06:23.771
A manifold question on whether Claude Opus 5.5 makes egregious errors sits at 75% implied probability on the board today,

00:06:24.311 --> 00:06:27.111
and that price is play money, mana, not dollars.

00:06:27.711 --> 00:06:33.871
Whether you can reach a venue and which contracts you can trade depends on the country, province, or state you live in,

00:06:34.171 --> 00:06:35.651
and those rules are still moving.

00:06:36.791 --> 00:06:42.191
Attendance, not the trophy, is the question on a new polymarket listing for the 2026 Ballendor

00:06:42.191 --> 00:06:42.691
ceremony.

00:06:43.151 --> 00:06:46.971
The page sets the night for October 26th at London's palladium.

00:06:47.511 --> 00:06:49.411
The first time the ceremony leaves Paris.

00:06:50.051 --> 00:06:54.211
It honors the 2025-2026 season, not the calendar year.

00:06:54.811 --> 00:07:00.151
The listing tells traders to watch club schedules, travel for nominees outside Europe, and late

00:07:00.151 --> 00:07:00.891
withdrawals.

00:07:01.767 --> 00:07:06.547
Kalshi has a contract on who becomes Trump's next press secretary, a reading at a

00:07:06.547 --> 00:07:14.927
1120 UTC on October 17th puts Scott Jennings at 20%, Annakelli at 13%, and Maria Barteromo

00:07:14.927 --> 00:07:16.047
at 5%.

00:07:16.047 --> 00:07:21.047
Those three names are not a full field, and the contract is about a job, not about

00:07:21.047 --> 00:07:21.867
who wins a race.

00:07:23.032 --> 00:07:27.632
A public wallet leaves a trail a reporter can follow, which is how it works when the trade

00:07:27.632 --> 00:07:29.392
sits on a chain anyone can read.

00:07:29.952 --> 00:07:32.672
The chain shows an address, a size, and a time.

00:07:33.212 --> 00:07:34.592
It does not show a legal name.

00:07:34.592 --> 00:07:39.352
claim. Clustering is the next move, and it is a guess that addresses funding one another

00:07:39.352 --> 00:07:45.912
or moving together, or run as a set. A cluster is not a person. An exchange pool, a shared

00:07:45.912 --> 00:07:50.752
treasury, or two operators on one signer will look like one actor until the path hits

00:07:50.752 --> 00:07:52.712
a service that mixes customer funds.

00:07:53.472 --> 00:08:00.572
rg.org, citing the anti-corruption data collective, reported that 10 wallets control 17% of congressional

00:08:00.572 --> 00:08:07.212
volume on polymarket. That is a concentration count. It does not identify 10 people, or one person,

00:08:07.412 --> 00:08:13.452
or anyone trading on private information. The same September 30 update found that 76% of

00:08:13.452 --> 00:08:20.992
those congressional markets hold less than $1,000. Among markets with a live book that day, 55.1%

00:08:20.992 --> 00:08:26.992
could be shoved 5 cents off the mid price for less than $1. Fewer than 1% of those books needed

00:08:26.992 --> 00:08:29.972
$10,000 or more to make the same kind of move.

00:08:30.452 --> 00:08:35.932
$5% matters because the contract pays at most a dollar, so a nickel is a large step on

00:08:35.932 --> 00:08:36.592
a shallow book.

00:08:37.252 --> 00:08:39.772
A big total and a shallow book can both be true.

00:08:40.312 --> 00:08:44.392
The total adds every trade, and the book is only what is resting at the current price.

00:08:45.052 --> 00:08:47.412
Both companies say they guard against misconduct.

00:08:47.972 --> 00:08:50.372
The wallet count and the shallow book measure shape.

00:08:50.892 --> 00:08:55.552
They do not, by themselves, prove manipulation, and they do not prove the venue's safeguards

00:08:55.552 --> 00:08:55.912
either.

00:08:55.912 --> 00:09:00.812
Follow a trade to a wallet and you have an address, a size, and a clock time.

00:09:01.412 --> 00:09:06.052
Calling that address a person or that size informed is a step the chain does not take.

